# Testing Rules (details in @docs/TESTING.md)

- Unit tests next to source: `*.service.spec.ts`. Mock repositories/external services.
- E2E in `test/e2e/*.e2e-spec.ts` against a real Postgres test DB (docker), migrations run before suite, truncate between tests.
- Structure: Arrange / Act / Assert; one behavior per test; descriptive names (`should reject booking when seat already held`).
- Must cover: happy path, validation errors, auth/ownership failures, and concurrency for booking.
- Concurrency test: fire N parallel requests for the same seat; exactly one succeeds.
- No real network calls; mock payment gateway and email.
- Don't weaken or delete a test to make it pass; fix the code or ask.
- Coverage targets: services ≥ 80%, booking/payment ≥ 90%.
- Report actual `npm run test` output when claiming completion.
